# Completion review

- Status card limits now count visible text after HTML parsing; boundary coverage includes escaped characters and emoji.

- Status separators use bold formatting throughout, model and reasoning level use a space, and emoji have no trailing space; updated status rendering checks.

- Registry change detection excludes the weekly limit and write time; the Kyiv clock follows daylight saving time and updates when the registry is written.

- Status evidence is prefetched within the root scope; active histories and recently inactive final messages stay bounded and partial collection is marked.

- Goal text is shown in an expandable block using the space remaining after the other status details; corrected the status-button check after removing the rate-limit footer.

- Reviewed the cumulative token calculation for all available descendants, including archived threads; incomplete totals are marked and the displayed subagent list remains bounded.

- Saved the topic ID and opening-message ID together, including after a database retry; failed sends leave the message ID empty.
- Verified with 1443 passing tests; Telegram deployment and existing-message ID import remain pending.
- Kept the context estimate and observed compaction count separate; made the edit path explicit and ensured cancelled journal readers terminate.
- Gateway event counts are lower bounds limited to the retained journal. Live Telegram rendering remains to be verified after deployment.
- The opening message uses durable, authorized buttons for questions and status; the pinned context is refreshed only after a consultant reply was delivered.
- Source-derived compaction events are counted from the retained gateway journal; the user chose to display the observed count without a lower-bound marker.
- The registry shows only an available weekly Codex limit, with a cached read and a bounded timeout; startup remains available before the daemon connects.

- Reviewed direct Telegram replies and recent thread snapshots; made the Codex client mandatory and simplified tool argument formatting. Existing opening messages receive the new button at startup.

- Reviewed grouped thread activity and bounded rollout reads; removed unused call metadata, confirmed tool outputs are excluded, and stabilized the startup test.

- Reviewed compact thread rendering: incoming agent messages use sender and recipient only, long tool calls remain separate, and collaboration message contents are never displayed.

- Reviewed compact thread formatting and completion events; consolidated grouped marker rendering while preserving separate expandable blocks.

- Reviewed uniform agent activity labels and single-entry truncation; simplified activity handling and verified grouped markers.

- Reviewed status evidence preprocessing and command formatting: encoded fragments are removed before truncation, command blocks stay separate, and interaction types retain bold formatting.

- Reviewed answer suffixes and thread snapshots; simplified suffix checks and verified compact replies, grouped calls, line caps, reasoning character counts, and collapsed waits.

- Reviewed pinned agent updates and the eight-agent limit; corrected rollout-fact test expectations for the increased limit.

- Reviewed paginated thread history and corrected a CI race by waiting for the fake Pico server to receive the stop message.
